+ * a few seconds and is kept across streams), so the extra frame comes one at a time (a 49-frame packet every ~52 ms
+ * at 48 kHz). The band's edges used to do it: 48-frame packets while the fill was under the top, then a burst of
+ * 49 once over it, every ~260 ms; a host that reads at the stream's average rate with a few frames in hand (an
+ * iPhone's camera) ran dry before each burst and filled in zeros, a click every ~250 ms while the sound played
+ * (tools/uac_stereo_test.c: what such a reader needs in hand). The band's edges, UA_GUARD further out, still act at
